license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Rectangles, solver, checker and paper for new best-known values of the balanced
  Latin rectangle problem. A simple simulated-annealing search improves 33 of the 51
  non-square instances (8 <= n <= 13) from Voboril, Peruvemba Ramaswamy and Szeider
  (CP 2025) and matches the other 18, beating each previous record after a median of
  0.12 CPU seconds on one laptop core. Every rectangle can be checked with an
  independent exact-arithmetic checker.
keywords:
  - Latin rectangles
  - spatially balanced Latin squares
  - combinatorial design
  - local search
  - simulated annealing
  - constraint programming
